---
import TimeSeries from '../../layouts/TimeSeries.astro';
import register from '../../../public/time-series/research-register.json';
const labs=[['weather','Weather, demand, and forecast uncertainty'],['signals','Latent signals, long-run relations, and breaks'],['geography','Geographic dependence and policy counterfactuals']];
---
<TimeSeries title="Research readings and replication paths" description="Primary papers, software, assumptions, failure experiments, and proposed research laboratories.">
  <header class="ea-hero"><div class="ea-hero-copy"><p class="ea-kicker">Research readings · reviewed {register.reviewed}</p><h1>What should we reproduce next?</h1><p class="ea-lead">A useful research exercise starts with a result we can check. Each reading below names an assumption to inspect, a calculation to reproduce, and a change that could break the argument.</p><p>The sixteen entries are study plans. Their paper replications have not yet been run here. The <a href="/time-series/code/">course calculations and Texas case</a> have separate execution records. Proposed extensions require further literature review before any claim of originality.</p><p><a href="/time-series/research-register.json" download>Download the source register ↓</a></p></div></header>
  {labs.map(([id,title])=><section class="ea-band"><h2>{title}</h2>{register.records.filter(r=>r.laboratory===id).map(r=><article class="ts-research-entry" id={r.id}><p class="ea-small">{r.citation} · {r.status}</p><h3><a href={r.paper}>{r.title}</a></h3><p>{r.question} {r.condition}</p><p><strong>Failure to investigate.</strong> {r.failure}</p><p><strong>Starting calculation.</strong> {r.replication}</p><p><strong>Proposed extension.</strong> {r.extension}</p>{r.software&&<p><a href={r.software}>Software or replication gateway ↗</a></p>}<details><summary>Source and reuse notes</summary><p>Paper: {r.paper_rights}</p><p>Code: {r.code_rights}</p><p>Data: {r.data_rights}</p>{r.doi&&<p>DOI: <a href={`https://doi.org/${r.doi}`}>{r.doi}</a></p>}</details></article>)}</section>)}
  <section class="ea-band ea-prose"><h2>A replication record</h2><p>Keep the paper version, software commit, package versions, input definitions, units, timestamps, transformations, and hashes with the result. Record the target before comparing estimators. A current-software example, an original-paper reproduction, and a reconstruction on another dataset answer different questions.</p><p>A failure belongs in the record too. A model that fails to converge, a forecast that lacks an available covariate, or a method that loses to its benchmark cannot quietly disappear from the comparison. Live assessments and grading keys are separate from these public research exercises.</p><p>Every laboratory begins with a model contract: the quantity of interest, information available at the decision, sampling unit, dependence and identification assumptions, uncertainty object, failure conditions, and the specific result to reproduce.</p></section>
</TimeSeries>
